  "full_response": "# **Slack Webhook Integration Guide**\nThis guide will help you set up and use **Incoming Webhooks** in Slack to send automated messages to a channel or user. Below, you'll find:\n\n1. **How to create a Slack webhook URL**\n2. **Example payloads** (including user mentions and channel IDs)\n3. **Best practices**\n\n---\n\n## **1. Setting Up a Slack Incoming Webhook**\n### **Step 1: Create a Slack App**\n1. Go to **[Slack API: Your Apps](https://api.slack.com/apps)**.\n2. Click **\"Create New App\"**.\n3. Choose **\"From scratch\"**, name your app, and select your workspace.\n4. Click **\"Create App\"**.\n\n### **Step 2: Enable Incoming Webhooks**\n1. In your app dashboard, go to **\"Incoming Webhooks\"**.\n2. Toggle **\"Activate Incoming Webhooks\"** to **On**.\n3. Click **\"Add New Webhook to Workspace\"**.\n4. Select the channel where messages should be posted (e.g., `#general` or a DM with a user).\n5. Click **\"Allow\"**.\n\n### **Step 3: Copy Your Webhook URL**\nAfter setup, you’ll see a **Webhook URL** like:\n```\nhttps://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n```\n⚠️ **Keep this URL secure!** Anyone with it can post messages to your Slack channel.\n\n---\n\n## **2. Example Payloads**\nSend a `POST` request to your webhook URL with a JSON payload.\n\n### **Basic Message**\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"Hello, Slack! :wave:\",\n  \"username\": \"Webhook Bot\",\n  \"icon_emoji\": \":robot_face:\"\n}\n```\n\n### **Message with User Mention**\nTo mention a user (`@username`), use their **Slack User ID** (e.g., `U12345678`).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"<@U12345678> Hey! A new update is available. :bell:\",\n  \"channel\": \"#general\"\n}\n```\n🔹 **How to find a User ID?**\n- Right-click a user → **\"Copy member ID\"**.\n\n### **Message with Channel Mention",
